{
    "background_story": "Richard was a former soldier who struggled to adjust to civilian life after returning from combat. The trauma he experienced during his tours of duty left him with a deep-seated sense of hostility, making it difficult for him to connect with others. He would often lash out at strangers, and his relationships with family and friends suffered as a result. Despite his best efforts, Richard found himself at odds with the world, always on the defensive and ready to strike. His hostility became a self-fulfilling prophecy, pushing away those who tried to help him and leaving him isolated and alone. It wasn't until he met a therapist who specialized in PTSD that Richard began to confront the demons that fueled his anger, slowly learning to channel his emotions into more positive outlets.",
